BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260903T223000Z
DTEND:20260904T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260903T000000Z
SUMMARY:History on the Hudson: 250 Years of Hudson County History - Battle of Bull's Ferry
DESCRIPTION:The Hudson County Office of Cultural and Heritage Affairs\, in 
 conjunction with the New Jersey Room of the Jersey City Free Public 
 Library\, presents a lecture series in celebration of the 250th Anniversary 
 of the Declaration of Independence. For five months across the Spring and 
 Summer of 2026\, we will spend the first Thursday evening with a speaker on 
 a wide range of Hudson County topics across our nation's first 250 
 years.\n\nFor the final event in the series\, on September 3\, Patrick 
 Cullen presents:\n\n\n\nWayne's 1780 Attack on the Blockhouse\n\nWest New 
 York historian Patrick Cullen will tell the story of Anthony Wayne's 
 unsuccessful attack on the blockhouse that residents loyal to the British 
 cause had constructed in what is now North Bergen and West New York. The 
 story sheds light on the contested role of the heavily wooded areas of 
 today's Hudson County as both side sought provisions in a "forage war."\n\n 
 \n\n
LOCATION:PGML: 3rd Floor | Conference Room 1
CATEGORIES:Popular Events
UID:LibCal-17419-16589540
URL:https://jclibrary.libcal.com/event/16589540
END:VEVENT
