SUMMARY:The Art of Salsa Dance - INTERMEDIATE
DESCRIPTION:\n\n\n\nThe Art of Salsa Dance - INTERMEDIATE\n\nThe Art of 
 Salsa Dance is back!\n\nThis Fall 2026\, join us on Wednesdays & select 
 Tuesdays for a fun and welcoming Salsa dance class where you’ll build 
 on:\n\n\n	\n	Essential On1 technique\n	\n	\n	Partner work\n	\n	\n	Shines 
 (solo footwork)\n	\n	\n	Musical foundations that shape the many styles of 
 salsa\n	\n\n\nAdvanced-Beginner / Intermediate Level: Previous knowledge 
 and understanding of the On1 basic step and partner work is needed\, 
 including commonly taught elements such as basic right turns and the 
 cross-body-lead. This class builds on the Beginner level\, moving at a 
 faster pace with a wider variety of partner combinations.\n\nAll classes 
 are open to adults and teens (ages 12 ). Please wear comfortable clothing 
 and shoes—and bring your energy!\n\nThe Art of Salsa Dance is a 
 community-rooted arts education program celebrating the cultural legacy of 
 Salsa born of migration\, resilience\, and musical innovation.\n\nTo learn 
 more about our other classes and events\, visit Keniadance.com/upcoming and 
 give us a follow @keniadance to stay up to date. \n\nThis program is 
 supported in part by public funds from the Jersey City Arts and Culture 
 Trust Fund and is presented by Kenia Rosete Dance in collaboration with 
 Jersey City Free Public Library\n\n
LOCATION:PGML - Fourth Floor Multipurpose Room
CATEGORIES:Popular Events > Music and Dance Events, September
