SUMMARY:Stage Play with Friends
DESCRIPTION:STAGE PLAY WITH FRIENDS In-Person\n\nSTAGE PLAY WITH FRIENDS is 
 Jersey City’s cold reading series for new works-in-progress. The 
 intention is to create a safe space where artists of all levels perform and 
 network with fellow artists\, and a vibrant and inclusive artist community 
 in Jersey City. STAGE PLAY WITH FRIENDS casts and presents excerpts of new 
 writing to an audience of fellow artists and supporters.\n\nWe have an open 
 submissions policy\, and host an open casting session at the start of each 
 event. We welcome prose\, solo work\, poetry\, plays\, screen plays\, tv 
 pilots\, sketches and music with written lyrics.\n\nThere will be 3-5 
 works-in-progress chosen from pre-submissions\, and 10 minutes will be 
 allotted to each. If your work was not chosen for the inaugural event\, it 
 will be considered for future readings. Actors\, arrive at 5:45 pm and 
 inform the creative director (Cynthia Cleto) you would like to be 
 considered for casting.\n\nFollow us on Instagram: 
 @stageplayjc\n\nSUBMISSIONS\n\nSubmit your work to: name@example.org 
 \n\nProse pieces: no more than 5 pages (12-point font\, double-spaced\, 1 
 inch margins)\n\nMulti-character dramatic pieces (i.e. plays and 
 screenplays): 10 pages maximum\, in a standard format (12-point font\, 
 double-spaced\, 1 inch margins)\n\nMusic: email song files to: 
 name@example.org \n\nInclude a front page that has: your name\, email 
 address and phone number. Please include: date of submission & a character 
 breakdown list. We will not accept adaptations of existing work.\n\nON THE 
 DAY OF THE EVENT \n\nWriters: please print the same number of copies of 
 your script as the number of performers. Include the “narrator” or 
 “stage direction” as a performer. Musicians: please bring any necessary 
 instruments or equipment (including amplifiers if needed).\n\nNOTE ABOUT 
 STAGE PLAY WITH FRIENDS\n\nWe are committed to fostering a respectful and 
 inclusive environment. Disrespectful behavior towards staff\, artists\, or 
 audience members will not be tolerated.
LOCATION:PGML: 3rd Floor | Conference Room 1
CATEGORIES:November, Popular Events, Popular Events > Educational Workshops, Popular Events > Social Gatherings, September
UID:LibCal-17419-17431785
URL:https://jclibrary.libcal.com/event/17431785
END:VEVENT
