SUMMARY:Books & Badges: Conversations That Matter
DESCRIPTION:Books & Badges: Conversations That Matter\n\nBooks & Badges: 
 Conversations That Matter is a community reading and discussion series 
 designed to bring residents\, teens\, and law enforcement together through 
 thoughtful conversation\, shared learning\, and the power of books.\n\nOpen 
 to ages 15 and up\, the series moves beyond casual introductions and 
 creates space for deeper conversations about leadership\, trust\, 
 identity\, communication\, public service\, belonging\, and community. Each 
 gathering uses reading as a starting point\, giving participants common 
 ideas and stories to reflect on before entering discussions that may 
 challenge perspectives\, encourage listening\, and build greater 
 understanding.\n\nRather than expecting everyone to agree\, Books & Badges 
 encourages participants to come with curiosity. Through guided 
 conversations\, community members and police leadership will have an 
 opportunity to exchange perspectives\, ask meaningful questions\, and 
 explore what it takes to strengthen relationships across 
 differences.\n\nRecommended Reading\n\nParticipants are encouraged to 
 explore the following featured selections:\n\nStart with Why: How Great 
 Leaders Inspire Everyone to Take Action by Simon Sinek\nA reflection on 
 purpose\, leadership\, and the values that inspire individuals and 
 organizations to serve others.\n\nBirmingham’s First Black in Blue by 
 Leroy Stover\nA powerful first-person account exploring race\, policing\, 
 perseverance\, leadership\, and institutional change through the 
 experiences of Birmingham’s first Black police officer.\n\nCrucial 
 Conversations: Tools for Talking When Stakes Are High by Joseph Grenny\, 
 Kerry Patterson\, Ron McMillan\, Al Switzler\, and Emily Gregory\nA 
 practical guide to communicating when opinions differ\, emotions are 
 strong\, and the conversation matters.\n\nThese recommended titles will be 
 available through Jersey City Free Public Library locations\, giving 
 community members the opportunity to read\, reflect\, and prepare before 
 attending a Books & Badges conversation.\n\nSee the full reading list here: 
 https://ww2.jclibrary.org/bookandbadgesreadinglist\n\nYou do not need to be 
 an expert\, agree with every idea in the books\, or have all the answers to 
 participate. Come ready to read\, listen\, share your perspective\, and 
 engage respectfully with your neighbors and local law 
 enforcement.\n\nBecause stronger communities are not built through one 
 conversation. They are built when we continue showing up\, learning from 
 one another\, and making room for conversations that matter.
LOCATION:PGML: 3rd Floor | Conference Room 1
CATEGORIES:December
UID:LibCal-17419-17358737
URL:https://jclibrary.libcal.com/event/17358737
